# LinguaPulse — deploy-time security headers.
# Netlify and Cloudflare Pages both read this file. When a CSP is delivered via
# an HTTP header it takes precedence over the <meta> CSP, so the full policy is
# reproduced here (plus frame-ancestors 'none' to block clickjacking) rather than
# just the added directive. Hosts that ignore _headers (e.g. GitHub Pages) fall
# back to the <meta> CSP, which still protects against XSS — only the
# frame-ancestors hardening is missing there.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https:; manifest-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
